From 9b7e34d0feb7a51680513ca62559459f122881e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:40:52 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] plan, adopt: take the recorded mode when pinned links
 hide it

read_snapshot classifies an adopted gadget from the functions linked next
to its pins. With ncm.usb0 pinned, charging_only, developer_mode and
tethering_mode all link nothing else, so developer mode read back as
charging_only. A switch to charging_only was then planned from
charging_only to charging_only and never stopped the developer service,
while the state file recorded charging_only.

classify now takes the pins and the mode the state file records. That
mode is used when the state file names the same gadget and configuration
and the links match the mode's composition without the pins; otherwise
the links decide, as before. This also covers developer and tethering,
which the state file already told apart, now only for the configuration
it records.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
