 The mode of an adopted gadget is read from the functions linked next to the
 pins: none is `charging_only`, `ncm.usb0` is `developer_mode` (or
-`tethering_mode`, if that was the last mode set). While any other function
+`tethering_mode`, if that was the last mode set). When the links match the
+composition of the mode that `state.env` records for the same gadget and
+configuration, that mode is used instead: with `ncm.usb0` pinned, for
+example, `charging_only`, `developer_mode` and `tethering_mode` link the same
+functions. While any other function
 that is neither pinned nor one of usb-signaller's own (`ncm.usb0`, `ffs.mtp`,
 `ffs.accessory`, `mass_storage.0`) is linked, mode switches are refused.
 
